<ESC>[2m<TS><ESC>[0m <ESC>[32m INFO<ESC>[0m kubeconfig invoked <ESC>[3mrefresh<ESC>[0m<ESC>[2m=<ESC>[0mtrue <ESC>[3myes<ESC>[0m<ESC>[2m=<ESC>[0mfalse
The age key at <SANDBOX>/home/.config/apprafter/age.key is missing, so nothing cached under it can be decrypted.
If you still have that key, put it back there, or set APPRAFTER_AGE_KEY to where it is, instead of going on.
Going on creates a new age key at <SANDBOX>/home/.config/apprafter/age.key, fetches the kubeconfig of target `prod` from its node again over SSH, and caches it under the new key. The new key cannot read what the lost one encrypted:
  - target `prod`: the Argo CD admin password, dropped from the cache (`apprafter argocd-password` fetches it from the cluster again)
  - target `staging`: the kubeconfig (`apprafter kubeconfig --refresh --target staging` fetches it again)
  - target `staging`: the Argo CD admin password (`apprafter argocd-password --refresh` fetches it again while `staging` is the active target)
